# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF, but without a policy git materialises CRLF on
# Windows, where `core.autocrlf` defaults to true. The formatting checks read
# files as checked out, so a CRLF working copy made `biome check` (and its
# predecessor's `--write`) report every file as misformatted on the Windows
# runners. Keep checkouts LF everywhere so the tools see what is committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# NSIS scripts are Windows-native and its samples ship CRLF; keep the checkout in
# the form the installer tooling expects (the repository copy stays LF).
*.nsi text eol=crlf
*.nsh text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never convert, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.avif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.zip binary
*.lockb binary
